## 2.6 Responsive behaviour

The same navigation hierarchy must work across all devices.

Desktop:
- Collapsible left navigation sidebar.
- Main content workspace.
- Utility area for search, notifications, XP and account controls.
- Optional contextual content panels.

Tablet:
- Compact or collapsible left navigation.
- Main workspace adapts to available width.
- Touch-friendly interactions.

Mobile:
- Collapsible left navigation opening as an overlay or drawer.
- Same navigation destinations and hierarchy as desktop.
- No separate bottom-navigation product structure.
- Main content uses available viewport width.
- Forms, uploads and dialogs adapt to narrow screens.

All devices must be supported in the initial release.

Responsive requirements:

- No horizontal overflow.
- No hover-only functionality.
- Touch-friendly controls.
- Appropriate text sizing.
- Mobile-friendly forms and uploads.
- Full-screen or adapted dialogs on narrow screens.
- Tables adapt to cards or horizontal scrolling.
- Mission actions remain accessible.
- Sidebar can open and close reliably.
- Search and notification utilities remain usable.

