## 6.2 Core relationships

- One account has one individual member profile.
- One individual may be associated with multiple organisations.
- One organisation can have multiple members.
- One member has one current membership status.
- One member has one current Ascendancy rank, with historical assignments retained.
- One member has one primary House and may have one secondary House.
- One House has many members and missions.
- One member may have multiple permission grants.
- One creator may create many missions.
- One mission may have many participants.
- One mission may have many submissions.
- One submission may have multiple evidence items.
- One submission may have multiple review events.
- An approved submission may create a contribution record.
- A contribution record may create an XP transaction and a CP event.
- One member may have many XP transactions.
- One member may earn many achievements.
- Leaderboard snapshots aggregate eligible CP events.
- Events and Academy completions may generate contribution records under their own rules.

## 6.3 Data integrity

The backend must enforce:

- Referential integrity.
- Unique identifiers.
- Valid status transitions.
- Permission checks.
- XP balance constraints.
- Duplicate prevention.
- Auditability.
- Correct ownership.
- Safe transaction handling.

Mission approval and XP settlement must be reliable under retries and concurrent operations.

