# 12. Acceptance criteria

Every MVP requirement must be tested against observable behaviour.

## 12.1 Account and membership

- A new individual can create one Arena account.
- Joining creates Spartan membership.
- Newbie is represented as onboarding state, not an account role.
- A member can select primary and secondary Houses.
- House affiliation does not automatically grant permissions.
- Leadership appointments are recorded separately from numerical level.

## 12.2 Navigation

- The same navigation destinations are available across supported devices.
- The left navigation can collapse and expand.
- On mobile it opens as a left-side drawer.
- No separate mobile bottom-navigation hierarchy is introduced.
- Search, notifications, Quick Create and account controls are accessible.
- Messaging is not presented as an available feature.

## 12.3 Missions

- An eligible member can create a mission.
- A creator without sufficient Spendable XP cannot publish a funded mission.
- Non-rewarded missions can be created where permitted.
- A participant can discover and join an eligible mission.
- A participant can submit required evidence.
- A reviewer can approve, reject or request revision.
- A member cannot approve their own submission.
- Approved submissions create contribution records.
- Mission budgets settle correctly.
- Unused funds are refunded according to the published rules.
- Disputes retain their history.

## 12.4 XP

- Lifetime XP and Spendable XP are separate.
- Spending XP does not reduce Lifetime XP.
- Mission funding reserves Spendable XP.
- Approved payouts create auditable transfers.
- Refunds restore available Spendable XP.
- Duplicate payouts are prevented.
- Balances cannot become negative.
- Numerical levels use Lifetime XP thresholds.
- XP thresholds are configurable.

## 12.5 Recognition and Leaderboards

- Achievements unlock only when criteria are satisfied.
- Achievements do not silently create duplicate XP awards.
- CP is separate from XP.
- CP cannot be spent or transferred.
- CP is awarded only for eligible verified contributions.
- Duplicate contribution scoring is prevented.
- Leaderboards use CP rather than Spendable XP.
- Seasonal and all-time records are distinguishable.
- House rankings respect House attribution.
- Privacy controls are respected.

## 12.6 Permissions

- Restricted tools are hidden from unauthorised members.
- Direct requests to protected operations are still rejected without permission.
- House managers are scoped to their assigned House.
- Reviewers cannot review their own submissions.
- Administrative actions are auditable.

## 12.7 Responsive behaviour

- Primary journeys work on desktop, tablet and mobile.
- The left navigation remains usable.
- Forms and uploads adapt to narrow screens.
- Mission details remain readable.
- No horizontal overflow is present.
- No important feature requires hover.

